Registration
------------

Not many people registered up to now. Please register as soon as possible i=
f you did not do so yet, so that I have a feeling who actually will come. I=
f you registered for the LF Summit and did not mention that you want to att=
end the OpenPrinting Summit, please post here. Post here also if you regist=
ered for the LF Summit and got rejected by the organization team of the LF =
Summit.


Participation by Phone
----------------------

If you will participate by call-in, please post here. So I know who I can e=
xpect to call in. If you call in only for a part of the session, please tel=
l to which sessions. You are not required by that to call in only on the sp=
ecified sessions. You can call in whenever you like. The conference phones =
are set up during the whole meeting.

Note that AFAIK call-in participation is only available for the OpenPrintin=
g Summit, not the other sessions of the LF Collaboration Summit.


Presentations
-------------

Please post here if you want to give a presentation. Upload your=20
presentation as PDF file to the OpenPrinting Summit web site and link it=20
from the appropriate session in the agenda.

It would be great to do this until March 31 so that we can talk about it=20
on the planning conference call. Please upload the presentation until=20
April 3 at the latest to give the atendees some preparation time for the=20
discussion. You can re-upload if you have updates.

Do not hesitate to give a presentation when you only participate by=20
call-in. We will show your slides while you are talking on the phone.=20
This worked great with Mike Sweet's presentation on the Printing Summit=20
in Lexington in 2006.

